{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"35770f3a","metadata":{"_kg_hide-input":true,"papermill":{"duration":0.009471,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:39.947802+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:39.938331+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(120deg, #0b1f4b 0%, #173d7a 38%, #2a78d6 72%, #eb6834 100%); padding: 32px 34px 28px 34px; border-radius: 14px; color: #ffffff;\">\n","<div style=\"font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: 0.85;\">Playground Series S6E11 &middot; Predicting Credit Card Fraud &middot; ROC-AUC</div>\n","<div style=\"font-size: 36px; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.12; margin-top: 10px;\">How much of the public top is real?</div>\n","<div style=\"font-size: 17px; margin-top: 8px; opacity: 0.95;\">Public ladders, their noise, the winner's curse, and the nested CV that tells you which steps will survive the private 80%</div>\n","<div style=\"margin-top: 18px;\">\n","<span style=\"background: #ffffff; color: #0b1f4b; border-radius: 12px; padding: 3px 11px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; margin-right: 6px;\">public LB = 20% of test</span>\n","<span style=\"background: #ffffff; color: #0b1f4b; border-radius: 12px; padding: 3px 11px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; margin-right: 6px;\">private = 80%</span>\n","<span style=\"background: #ffffff; color: #0b1f4b; border-radius: 12px; padding: 3px 11px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; margin-right: 6px;\">nested CV</span>\n","<span style=\"background: rgba(255,255,255,0.18); color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 3px 11px; font-size: 12px; margin-right: 6px;\">every number computed here</span>\n","<span style=\"background: rgba(255,255,255,0.18); color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 3px 11px; font-size: 12px; margin-right: 6px;\">public inputs only, SHA-256 checked</span>\n","<span style=\"background: rgba(255,255,255,0.18); color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 3px 11px; font-size: 12px;\">CPU, ~15 min</span>\n","</div>\n","</div>\n","\n","The top of the public board is a dense band of files a few hundred-thousandths apart. Many of them are **ladders**:\n","a strong public file plus small steps, each kept because the public score went up by one or two points\n","(1 point = 0.00001 AUC). But the public score is computed on only ~60,000 rows with about a thousand frauds. This\n","notebook measures, with public files only, **how big the noise of one such step is, how much of a ladder's gain\n","nested CV confirms, and how much of the top band is likely to move on the private 80%**. It takes no side: the ladder\n","authors themselves list every probe and check their steps on CV, which is what makes this analysis possible.\n","\n","<div style=\"background: #fff4ec; border-left: 5px solid #eb6834; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 6px 0;\">\n","<b>New in v4 (14 Nov).</b><br>\n","&bull; <a href=\"#s8\">The board, 12 &rarr; 14 Nov</a>: the band rose; #1 sits far outside any public-noise range.<br>\n","&bull; <a href=\"#s9\">The two new top ladders</a> (goodpjw2008's <i>Public and CV Up</i>, 0.95386, and Areeb Ali's <i>Bold, Then Bolder</i>, 0.95388)\n","rebuilt from public files: every probe, its noise, its OOF change, and its expected private value.<br>\n","&bull; <a href=\"#s10\">\"Public and CV up\", checked fold by fold</a>, with a nested choice of the last step size.<br>\n","&bull; <a href=\"#s11\">Error analysis</a>: which rows the top files fight over, by score band, amount and channel.<br>\n","&bull; <a href=\"#s12\">An honest extension of the best public file</a>: up to two steps, chosen by nested CV only. Result: no step\n","passes, so <code>submission.csv</code> is the plain, credited rebuild of the 0.95388 file.\n","</div>\n","\n","<div style=\"background: #eef4fc; border-left: 5px solid #2a78d6; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 6px 0;\">\n","<b>Contents</b><br>\n","<a href=\"#ack\">0. Acknowledgements and who did what</a><br>\n","<a href=\"#hero\">The whole story in one figure</a><br>\n","<a href=\"#s1\">1. The competition in five minutes</a> &mdash; data, AUC, how big the public and private parts are<br>\n","<a href=\"#s2\">2. How noisy is the public LB?</a> &mdash; one file versus the difference of two files, and a one-line rule<br>\n","<a href=\"#s3\">3. Anatomy of a ladder</a> &mdash; every public rung against its noise and against nested CV<br>\n","<a href=\"#s4\">4. The winner's curse</a> &mdash; why the best of many probes looks better than it is<br>\n","<a href=\"#s5\">5. CV can be tuned too</a> &mdash; early stopping on the scored fold, selection on the reported folds, tests inside one fold<br>\n","<a href=\"#s6\">6. What did not work</a><br>\n","<a href=\"#s7\">7. What to expect on private, and how to pick two final files</a><br>\n","<a href=\"#s8\">8. New: the board, 12 &rarr; 14 November</a><br>\n","<a href=\"#s9\">9. New: anatomy of the two new ladders</a> &mdash; and what each new notebook's public tuning is likely to cost on private<br>\n","<a href=\"#s10\">10. New: \"public and CV up\", checked fold by fold</a><br>\n","<a href=\"#s11\">11. New: error analysis on the OOF rows</a><br>\n","<a href=\"#s12\">12. New: one honest step on top of the best public file?</a> &mdash; this notebook's <code>submission.csv</code><br>\n","<a href=\"#s13\">13. Full credits and licences</a>\n","</div>\n","\n","If this is useful to you, an upvote helps others find it. Corrections are very welcome in the comments."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"526eead4","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.00746,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:39.962324+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:39.954864+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"setup\"></a>\n","<div style=\"background: #0b1f4b; color: #ffffff; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700;\">Setup &middot; public inputs, checked byte for byte</div>\n","\n","Every input is a public file: the competition data, public OOF/test predictions and two public ladder base files.\n","Each one is found anywhere under `/kaggle/input` by name and checked by its SHA-256 (the `find()` idea is\n","goodpjw2008's). The notebook runs on CPU in about ten minutes and never trains a big model."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"c5f64d91","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:19:39.978014Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:19:39.977673Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.202976Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.200772Z"},"papermill":{"duration":9.237108,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.206391+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:39.969283+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[ 0.1 min] train 699,960 rows, fraud rate 1.6700%; test 299,984 rows\n"]}],"source":["# Imports, input discovery by SHA-256, the shared scale for predictions, and a fast AUC for repeated random splits.\n","import os, time, hashlib, warnings, math\n","from pathlib import Path\n","import numpy as np, pandas as pd\n","from scipy.stats import rankdata, norm\n","from scipy.special import logit\n","from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\n","from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold\n","from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n","T0 = time.time()\n","def log(*a): print(f\"[{(time.time() - T0) / 60:4.1f} min]\", *a, flush=True)\n","\n","INPUT = Path(os.environ.get(\"KAGGLE_INPUT\", \"/kaggle/input\"))\n","WORK = Path(os.environ.get(\"KAGGLE_WORKING\", \"/kaggle/working\"))\n","_sha = {}\n","def sha256(p):\n","    p = Path(p)\n","    if p not in _sha: _sha[p] = hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n","    return _sha[p]\n","\n","def find(names, digest=None, inside=None, required=True):\n","    \"\"\"A file anywhere under /kaggle/input, by (one of its) names and, if given, its SHA-256.\n","    If no file has the expected hash but one has the name, use it and say so (the author may have updated it).\"\"\"\n","    names = [names] if isinstance(names, str) else names\n","    hits = [p for n in names for p in sorted(INPUT.rglob(n)) if inside is None or inside in str(p)]\n","    good = [p for p in hits if digest is None or sha256(p) == digest]\n","    if good: return good[0]\n","    if hits:\n","        print(f\"  NOTE: {names[0]} found but its SHA-256 differs from the one this notebook was written with; numbers may differ slightly.\")\n","        return hits[0]\n","    if required: raise FileNotFoundError(names)\n","    print(f\"  NOTE: {names[0]} not attached; the cells that need it are skipped.\")\n","    return None\n","\n","def L(v):\n","    \"\"\"Logit rank: AUC only sees order, so every prediction goes on one scale (as the public ladders do).\"\"\"\n","    return logit((rankdata(v) - 0.5) / len(v))\n","\n","# daoviet removed his GP + DVAE OOF/test files from his dataset on 13 Nov; Aman Atar's q17 bundle carries the same\n","# predictions (identical ranks, checked below by a hash of the ranks), so they are read from there when needed.\n","GPD_IN_BUNDLE = {\"oof_ours.npy\": (\"oof_daoviet_gpdvae\", \"1c7c7fa5e49aaf8f6f63f40bb258bdff864dd49f15239fa10bb2a9c55b800688\"),\n","                 \"test_ours.npy\": (\"test_daoviet_gpdvae\", \"10f7dec317a923cc4bb67b3aff770db528abd330b53da8c53be23e8b636d050d\")}\n","def load(names, digest, required=True):\n","    nm = names if isinstance(names, str) else names[0]\n","    if nm in GPD_IN_BUNDLE and not any(sha256(q) == digest for q in INPUT.rglob(nm)):\n","        key, rank_sha = GPD_IN_BUNDLE[nm]\n","        v = np.load(find(\"rank1_q17_streams.npz\", \"0fe4ab1263a673c8065d7145590b92da440263161bf860ce45f2976b5c4fa56f\"), allow_pickle=False)[key].astype(np.float64)\n","        assert hashlib.sha256(rankdata(v).tobytes()).hexdigest() == rank_sha, \"bundle copy of GP + DVAE differs in rank order\"\n","        print(f\"  {nm}: read from Aman Atar's q17 bundle ({key}); rank order identical to daoviet's original file\")\n","        return v\n","    p = find(names, digest, required=required)\n","    return None if p is None else np.load(p, allow_pickle=False).astype(np.float64)\n","\n","def auc_prep(score):\n","    \"\"\"Pre-sort a score once: the negatives in score order, and for every positive the number of negatives below it.\"\"\"\n","    o = np.argsort(score, kind=\"stable\"); yo = y[o]\n","    neg_o = o[~yo].astype(np.int32); pos_rows = o[yo].astype(np.int32)\n","    kpos = np.cumsum(~yo)[yo].astype(np.int32)\n","    return neg_o, pos_rows, kpos\n","\n","def auc_counts(prep, counts, denom):\n","    \"\"\"AUC on a bootstrap sample (counts[i] = how often row i was drawn): O(n) per sample, no sort (ties ignored).\"\"\"\n","    neg_o, pos_rows, kpos = prep\n","    cn = np.concatenate(([0], np.cumsum(counts[neg_o], dtype=np.int64)))\n","    return float((counts[pos_rows].astype(np.int64) * cn[kpos]).sum()) / denom\n","\n","def auc_sort(yr, s):\n","    \"\"\"Plain AUC by one sort (Mann-Whitney), ~3x faster than sklearn on 700k rows; ties ignored.\"\"\"\n","    idx = np.flatnonzero(yr[np.argsort(s, kind=\"stable\")]); npos = len(idx)\n","    return (idx.sum() - npos * (npos - 1) / 2) / (npos * (len(yr) - npos))\n","\n","COMP = \"playground-series-s6e11\"\n","train = pd.read_csv(find(\"train.csv\", inside=COMP))\n","test_ids = pd.read_csv(find(\"test.csv\", inside=COMP), usecols=[\"id\"])[\"id\"].to_numpy()\n","sample = pd.read_csv(find(\"sample_submission.csv\", inside=COMP))\n","y = train[\"is_fraud\"].to_numpy().astype(bool)\n","FOLDS = [b for _, b in StratifiedKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=42).split(y, y)]   # the split every public OOF uses\n","N, NT = len(y), len(test_ids)\n","log(f\"train {N:,} rows, fraud rate {y.mean():.4%}; test {NT:,} rows\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"ec664fa0","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.236547Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.236042Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.262072Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.261024Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.04454,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.264653+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.220113+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# One style for every figure: a colorblind-checked palette with fixed roles, recessive axes, titles that state the\n","# takeaway, KPI tiles, and the helpers that place text without clutter.\n","from matplotlib.patches import FancyBboxPatch, Patch\n","from matplotlib.lines import Line2D\n","from matplotlib.ticker import FuncFormatter, MaxNLocator\n","INK, INK2, MUTED, RULE, SURF, PAGE, NAVY = \"#0b0b0b\", \"#52514e\", \"#8a8984\", \"#d6d5d0\", \"#fcfcfb\", \"#f9f9f7\", \"#0b1f4b\"\n","C = [\"#2a78d6\", \"#eb6834\", \"#1baf7a\", \"#eda100\", \"#e87ba4\", \"#008300\", \"#6250d6\", \"#e34948\"]\n","PUB, PRIV, CV, BAND = C[0], C[1], C[2], \"#e6e5df\"      # fixed roles: public = blue, private = orange, CV = aqua\n","CVTXT = \"#0f7a55\"                                        # darker aqua for text next to aqua marks\n","plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.facecolor\": PAGE, \"axes.facecolor\": SURF, \"savefig.facecolor\": PAGE, \"axes.edgecolor\": \"#c3c2b7\",\n","                     \"axes.labelcolor\": INK2, \"xtick.color\": INK2, \"ytick.color\": INK2, \"axes.grid\": True,\n","                     \"grid.color\": \"#e8e7e3\", \"grid.linewidth\": 0.7, \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n","                     \"font.family\": \"DejaVu Sans\", \"font.size\": 10, \"axes.titlesize\": 11.5, \"axes.titleweight\": \"bold\",\n","                     \"axes.titlecolor\": INK, \"axes.titlelocation\": \"left\", \"axes.titlepad\": 10, \"lines.linewidth\": 2,\n","                     \"legend.frameon\": False, \"axes.axisbelow\": True, \"figure.dpi\": 110, \"xtick.labelsize\": 9, \"ytick.labelsize\": 9})\n","E5 = FuncFormatter(lambda v, _: f\"{v:+g}\" if v else \"0\")    # axis ticks in units of 1e-5 AUC\n","\n","def headline(fig, title, sub=None, top_pad=0.0):\n","    \"\"\"Figure title that states the takeaway (left aligned), with an optional grey subtitle.\"\"\"\n","    h = fig.get_figheight()\n","    fig.text(0.012, 1 - 0.12 / h, title, ha=\"left\", va=\"top\", fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK)\n","    if sub: fig.text(0.012, 1 - 0.46 / h, sub, ha=\"left\", va=\"top\", fontsize=10, color=INK2)\n","    fig.tight_layout(rect=(0, 0, 1, 1 - ((0.80 if sub else 0.50) + top_pad) / h))\n","\n","def tile(fig, rect, label, value, note, color=NAVY):\n","    \"\"\"A KPI tile: label, big value, small note, with a coloured accent bar.\"\"\"\n","    ax = fig.add_axes(rect); ax.set_axis_off()\n","    ax.add_patch(FancyBboxPatch((0, 0), 1, 1, boxstyle=\"round,pad=0,rounding_size=0.08\", transform=ax.transAxes,\n","                                facecolor=SURF, edgecolor=\"#e6e5df\", lw=1.2))\n","    ax.add_patch(FancyBboxPatch((0, 0.10), 0.018, 0.80, boxstyle=\"round,pad=0,rounding_size=0.01\", transform=ax.transAxes,\n","                                facecolor=color, edgecolor=\"none\"))\n","    ax.text(0.07, 0.76, label, transform=ax.transAxes, fontsize=9.5, color=INK2, va=\"center\")\n","    ax.text(0.07, 0.45, value, transform=ax.transAxes, fontsize=20, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK, va=\"center\")\n","    ax.text(0.07, 0.15, note, transform=ax.transAxes, fontsize=8.5, color=MUTED, va=\"center\")\n","\n","def panel_title(ax, title, sub=None):\n","    ax.set_title(title, loc=\"left\", fontsize=11.5, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK, pad=22 if sub else 8)\n","    if sub: ax.text(0, 1.02, sub, transform=ax.transAxes, fontsize=9, color=INK2, va=\"bottom\")\n","\n","def zero_line(ax, axis=\"y\"):\n","    (ax.axhline if axis == \"y\" else ax.axvline)(0, color=\"#b9b8b3\", lw=1, zorder=1)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c3dd985a","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.009391,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.28187+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.272479+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**How the numbers below are made.** The test labels are hidden, so we use the next best thing: the **nested OOF of\n","goodpjw2008's public wide LM stack** (Part 12, AUC 0.9526 on 699,960 training rows). It is a real top-band\n","prediction with honest out-of-fold scores. We draw hundreds of random public parts (~60k rows) and private parts\n","(~240k rows) from it, as two parts of a fresh test set would be drawn, and watch how scores move. Every ladder step that has public OOF files\n","behind it is applied to the same OOF, exactly as the ladder authors did in their own CV checks."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"8b121a36","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.303039Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.3027Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:20:02.439129Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:20:02.437942Z"},"papermill":{"duration":13.147588,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:20:02.441551+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:19:49.293963+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  oof_ours.npy: read from Aman Atar's q17 bundle (oof_daoviet_gpdvae); rank order identical to daoviet's original file\n","  W    OOF AUC 0.952565   goodpjw2008, wide LM stack (nested OOF)\n","  LM   OOF AUC 0.950428   megayak, target-first LM\n","  L7F  OOF AUC 0.949448   goodpjw2008, compact LM seed 7\n","  GPD  OOF AUC 0.946489   daoviet, GP + DVAE\n","  MLP  OOF AUC 0.951223   goodpjw2008, OOF bank MLP bag\n","  GB   OOF AUC 0.951506   goodpjw2008, OOF bank GB bag\n","  MS   OOF AUC 0.950027   masayakawamata, target-first GPT-2\n","  G26  OOF AUC 0.950140   goodpjw2008, GPT-2 seed 2026\n","[ 0.2 min] wide LM stack, nested CV 0.952565\n","[ 0.3 min] OOF bank: 20 core members loaded\n"]}],"source":["# Load the public OOF predictions (train side). W = the nested OOF of the public wide LM stack.\n","OOF_FILES = {   # key: (file name(s), SHA-256, who published it)\n","    \"W\":   (\"wide_lm_stack_nested.npy\", \"69375871698f1adf2b4c666fc7f5180edf00ac6836668353b8e7e4ca43eb2722\", \"goodpjw2008, wide LM stack (nested OOF)\"),\n","    \"LM\":  ([\"lm_oof.npy\", \"megalm_oof_sha181c.npy\"], \"181ceac8f3a48fcf9a1702e1222ee13178f0688a28c1aff22c8f881532ea981a\", \"megayak, target-first LM\"),\n","    \"L7F\": (\"lm7_oof_5fold.npy\", \"c56d6b7282e7ea8c4c5927ac27e8b286d539ffbd66d5795564323c8b92b65242\", \"goodpjw2008, compact LM seed 7\"),\n","    \"GPD\": (\"oof_ours.npy\", \"91be476ddb00fe1232ba98b9a30f3c6215e81769499e3594058e4e99703c706a\", \"daoviet, GP + DVAE\"),\n","    \"MLP\": (\"oof_gbn_bag5_w512.npy\", \"e8ef910425641b7be8f3bf8f964b1637e9fa39937a772df56ef0cb660d3776f3\", \"goodpjw2008, OOF bank MLP bag\"),\n","    \"GB\":  (\"oof_gb_bag5.npy\", \"4b4bc47571ee389a54a7e70d6ac2d716207c329a1ca619a37e577de1f30aea40\", \"goodpjw2008, OOF bank GB bag\"),\n","    \"MS\":  (\"oof.npy\", \"3468aaaeb7851739ec0de1e06b780da6d2777fcaeef638a6852c56e68e67a206\", \"masayakawamata, target-first GPT-2\"),\n","    \"G26\": (\"gpt2_s2026_oof_5fold.npy\", \"4a902ecd3d725d21123f5b6239ac2190a9fd94f3de37e3157be391fcf3fe996a\", \"goodpjw2008, GPT-2 seed 2026\"),\n","}\n","O = {k: L(load(n, h)) for k, (n, h, _) in OOF_FILES.items()}\n","W = O[\"W\"]\n","def cv(s): return np.mean([roc_auc_score(y[b], s[b]) for b in FOLDS])\n","def folds_up(s, base): return sum(roc_auc_score(y[b], s[b]) > roc_auc_score(y[b], base[b]) for b in FOLDS)\n","CV_W = cv(W)\n","for k in O: print(f\"  {k:4s} OOF AUC {roc_auc_score(y, O[k]):.6f}   {OOF_FILES[k][2]}\")\n","log(f\"wide LM stack, nested CV {CV_W:.6f}\")\n","\n","# The OOF bank's 20 'core' members (one per recipe), used as extra probe directions and for the hill-climbing demo.\n","bank_dir = find(\"manifest.csv\", inside=\"oof-bank\").parent\n","bank_man = pd.read_csv(bank_dir / \"manifest.csv\")\n","CORE = [n for n in bank_man.loc[bank_man[\"core\"], \"name\"] if (bank_dir / f\"oof_{n}.npy\").exists()]\n","BANK = {n: L(np.load(bank_dir / f\"oof_{n}.npy\", allow_pickle=False).astype(np.float64)) for n in CORE}\n","log(f\"OOF bank: {len(BANK)} core members loaded\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"26a532aa","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:20:02.46Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:20:02.459555Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:20:29.684701Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:20:29.683867Z"},"papermill":{"duration":27.236902,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:20:29.68719+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:20:02.450288+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[ 0.3 min] 35 moves to score\n","[ 0.8 min] nested-CV change of every move computed\n"]}],"source":["# Every public probe that has OOF files behind it, applied to W as a move  W + w * direction.\n","# 'pub' = the public-LB change the authors report for that single step (x 1e-5), with the source.\n","MOVES = [  # (short name, direction on the OOF, reported public change, source)\n","    (\"+0.12 megayak LM\",          0.12 * (O[\"LM\"] - W),                       +1, \"goodpjw2008 v1: 0.95342 -> 0.95343\"),\n","    (\"+0.06 seed-7 LM\",           0.06 * (O[\"L7F\"] - W),                      +2, \"goodpjw2008 v1: 0.95343 -> 0.95345\"),\n","    (\"+0.12 public GPT-2\",        0.12 * (O[\"MS\"] - W),                      -14, \"goodpjw2008 v1 probe: -14 points\"),\n","    (\"+0.05 GP + DVAE\",           0.05 * (O[\"GPD\"] - W),                      +3, \"daoviet: 0.95348 -> 0.95351\"),\n","    (\"LM weight 0.12 -> 0.09\",   -0.03 * (O[\"LM\"] - W),                       +1, \"Areeb Ali v19: 0.95347 -> 0.95348\"),\n","    (\"more of both LMs\",          0.04 * (O[\"LM\"] - W) + 0.03 * (O[\"L7F\"] - W), -2, \"Areeb Ali probe: 0.95347 -> 0.95345\"),\n","    (\"less seed-7 LM\",           -0.02 * (O[\"L7F\"] - W),                       0, \"Areeb Ali probe: 0.95347 -> 0.95347\"),\n","    (\"GPT-2 seed swap 0.06\",      0.06 * (O[\"G26\"] - O[\"MS\"]),                +2, \"goodpjw2008 v2: 0.95352 -> 0.95354\"),\n","    (\"GPT-2 seed swap 0.10\",      0.10 * (O[\"G26\"] - O[\"MS\"]),                +2, \"goodpjw2008 v2 probe: 0.95354\"),\n","]\n","TREE = -0.10 * (O[\"MLP\"] - W) - 0.05 * (O[\"GB\"] - W)        # Areeb Ali's full tree move (v15); no clean single-step public number\n","# A family of plausible probes: a small step towards (or away from) each bank member and each public LM.\n","rng = np.random.default_rng(11)\n","FAMILY = []\n","for name, X in list(BANK.items()) + [(\"megayak LM\", O[\"LM\"]), (\"seed-7 LM\", O[\"L7F\"]), (\"public GPT-2\", O[\"MS\"]),\n","                                     (\"GPT-2 seed 2026\", O[\"G26\"]), (\"GP + DVAE\", O[\"GPD\"])]:\n","    w = rng.choice([-0.10, -0.06, -0.03, 0.03, 0.06, 0.10])\n","    FAMILY.append((f\"{w:+.2f} {name}\", w * (X - W)))\n","SCORES = [(\"base\", np.zeros(N))] + [(m[0], m[1]) for m in MOVES] + [(\"tree move\", TREE)] + FAMILY\n","log(f\"{len(SCORES) - 1} moves to score\")\n","\n","RHO, TRUE, UP = {}, {}, {}\n","RW = rankdata(W)\n","for name, d in SCORES[1:]:\n","    s = W + d\n","    RHO[name] = np.corrcoef(rankdata(s), RW)[0, 1]\n","    TRUE[name] = (cv(s) - CV_W) * 1e5\n","    UP[name] = folds_up(s, W)\n","log(\"nested-CV change of every move computed\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"077a5ca0","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:20:29.705597Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:20:29.704888Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:23:57.868481Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:23:57.867615Z"},"papermill":{"duration":208.180913,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:23:57.876277+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:20:29.695364+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[ 2.0 min]   100 of 300 splits\n","[ 3.1 min]   200 of 300 splits\n","[ 4.2 min]   300 of 300 splits\n","[ 4.2 min] one file: public AUC SD 0.00334, public-minus-private SD 0.00362; rule K = 0.0047\n"]}],"source":["# Random public/private splits: the public part is a bootstrap sample of NPUB rows from the OOF, the private part an\n","# independent bootstrap sample of the other NT - NPUB rows (independent draws, as two parts of a fresh test set would be).\n","R = int(os.environ.get(\"NB_DRAWS\", 300))\n","NPUB = int(round(0.2 * NT))\n","preps = [auc_prep(W + d) for _, d in SCORES]\n","AUC = np.zeros((len(SCORES), R, 2))\n","rng = np.random.default_rng(2026)\n","for r in range(R):\n","    cp = np.bincount(rng.integers(0, N, NPUB), minlength=N).astype(np.int32)\n","    cq = np.bincount(rng.integers(0, N, NT - NPUB), minlength=N).astype(np.int32)\n","    dp = float(cp[y].sum()) * float(cp[~y].sum()); dq = float(cq[y].sum()) * float(cq[~y].sum())\n","    for i, pr in enumerate(preps):\n","        AUC[i, r, 0] = auc_counts(pr, cp, dp); AUC[i, r, 1] = auc_counts(pr, cq, dq)\n","    if r % 100 == 99: log(f\"  {r + 1} of {R} splits\")\n","del preps\n","DELTA = (AUC[1:] - AUC[:1]) * 1e5           # (move, draw, public/private) change vs the base file, in 1e-5\n","NAMES = [n for n, _ in SCORES[1:]]\n","SD_PUB = DELTA[:, :, 0].std(1); SD_PRV = DELTA[:, :, 1].std(1)\n","AGREE = (np.sign(DELTA[:, :, 0]) == np.sign(DELTA[:, :, 1])).mean(1)\n","ONE_RHO = np.array([1 - RHO[n] for n in NAMES])\n","K_RULE = np.exp(np.mean(np.log(SD_PUB * 1e-5 / np.sqrt(ONE_RHO))))   # sigma_public(delta) ~= K_RULE * sqrt(1 - rho)\n","SD_BASE_PUB, SD_BASE_GAP = AUC[0, :, 0].std(), (AUC[0, :, 0] - AUC[0, :, 1]).std()\n","log(f\"one file: public AUC SD {SD_BASE_PUB:.5f}, public-minus-private SD {SD_BASE_GAP:.5f}; rule K = {K_RULE:.4f}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"541b05a1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:23:58.032406Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:23:58.032055Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:24:04.109591Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:24:04.108368Z"},"papermill":{"duration":6.088713,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:24:04.111674+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:23:58.022961+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  test_ours.npy: read from Aman Atar's q17 bundle (test_daoviet_gpdvae); rank order identical to daoviet's original file\n","rebuilt 0.95354 file identical to the published one: True\n","  Strike 10 (amanatar)             public +10e-5   1-rho 2.25e-04   noise SD of the public gap ~7.0e-5\n","  + 0.6 (S10 - S9)                 public  +2e-5   1-rho 8.10e-05   noise SD of the public gap ~4.2e-5\n","  + 0.12 megayak LM                public  +1e-5   1-rho 3.64e-04   noise SD of the public gap ~8.9e-5\n","  0.95352 file (several steps)     public  +9e-5   1-rho 4.11e-04   noise SD of the public gap ~9.5e-5\n","  + 0.06 GPT-2 seed swap           public  +2e-5   1-rho 3.09e-05   noise SD of the public gap ~2.6e-5\n","[ 4.3 min] typical noise of one rung on the public board: 7.0e-5\n"]}],"source":["# Rebuild the public ladder files on the TEST set from the authors' public inputs (formulas copied from their notebooks),\n","# and measure how different consecutive rungs are (rank correlation). The last file is checked byte for byte against\n","# the published 0.95354 output (Areeb Ali's notebook asserts the same SHA-256).\n","TEST_FILES = {\n","    \"A\":   (\"submission_095340.csv\", \"12b525b84f29e32d6511e9d6105f6dc5eac79ae41b10140eed3353ea57afc159\"),   # Strike 10, amanatar\n","    \"F\":   (\"submission_095330.csv\", \"f4a7a4f8636c99fabd82945c7d81956c5559c609dcb55cde6d4e03f80b0ea105\"),   # Strike 9, Moran Z\n","    \"LM\":  ([\"lm_test.npy\", \"megalm_test_sha3168.npy\"], \"3168779be644a530c6bdc4c141cae168bfc2feb01ac21090c917cc978a7687d3\"),\n","    \"L7F\": (\"lm7_test_5fold.npy\", \"68639fec79f081e97d40185443fa3903c9db3e62698abb01dfe31dcee217462a\"),\n","    \"GPD\": (\"test_ours.npy\", \"96f3bdde816e604438e61eac9722f7a7402f1c39bb8efe8999793b23f91d02f2\"),\n","    \"MLP\": (\"test_gbn_bag5_w512.npy\", \"035d6544d7c03108fc42ee296a8660a45825e3b1b19b7cabce1c3f42cac4e7cb\"),\n","    \"GB\":  (\"test_gb_bag5.npy\", \"7d54e5f17e0707d88fec1a2cccb05885978ae6cc2a595c5f4575c7b7d45a9bb8\"),\n","    \"MS\":  (\"test.npy\", \"6c27aff7be744f7a0cc17809e0cd04fcdea0664234af88e3040a25235fb67906\"),\n","    \"G26\": (\"gpt2_s2026_test_f0.npy\", \"40e08058ed7632ee328c2fe7d97040b856b36d2636f32cc6d2781ec9db080695\"),\n","}\n","T = {}\n","for k, (n, h) in TEST_FILES.items():\n","    if isinstance(n, str) and n in GPD_IN_BUNDLE: T[k] = L(load(n, h)); continue\n","    p = find(n, h, required=False)\n","    if p is None: continue\n","    if str(p).endswith(\".csv\"):\n","        d = pd.read_csv(p); assert (d[\"id\"].to_numpy() == sample[\"id\"].to_numpy()).all(); T[k] = L(d[\"is_fraud\"].to_numpy())\n","    else: T[k] = L(np.load(p, allow_pickle=False).astype(np.float64))\n","HAVE_LADDER = len(T) == len(TEST_FILES)\n","RUNGS = []   # (label, test-file score, reported public LB)\n","if HAVE_LADDER:\n","    A, F = T[\"A\"], T[\"F\"]\n","    a2 = A + 0.6 * (A - F)\n","    a3 = a2 + 0.12 * (T[\"LM\"] - F)\n","    s352 = A + 0.6 * (A - F) + 0.09 * (T[\"LM\"] - F) + 0.09 * (T[\"L7F\"] - F) + 0.05 * (T[\"GPD\"] - F) - 0.05 * (T[\"MLP\"] - F) - 0.025 * (T[\"GB\"] - F)\n","    s354 = L(s352) + 0.06 * (T[\"G26\"] - T[\"MS\"])\n","    s354b = L(s352) + 0.10 * (T[\"G26\"] - T[\"MS\"])\n","    out = (rankdata(s354) - 0.5) / NT\n","    chk = WORK / \"rebuild_095354.csv\"; sample[[\"id\"]].assign(is_fraud=out).to_csv(chk, index=False)\n","    print(\"rebuilt 0.95354 file identical to the published one:\", sha256(chk) == \"1e2e72fa26309ce630a19e0df780ae63d525901f33dc23f9058581ced5e9d6e0\")\n","    RUNGS = [(\"Strike 9 (Moran Z)\", F, 95330), (\"Strike 10 (amanatar)\", A, 95340), (\"+ 0.6 (S10 - S9)\", a2, 95342),\n","             (\"+ 0.12 megayak LM\", a3, 95343), (\"0.95352 file (several steps)\", s352, 95352),\n","             (\"+ 0.06 GPT-2 seed swap\", s354, 95354)]\n","    rk = {lab: rankdata(s) for lab, s, _ in RUNGS}\n","    STEPS = []   # (label, public gain e-5, 1 - rho vs previous rung, predicted public noise SD e-5)\n","    for (l0, _, p0), (l1, _, p1) in zip(RUNGS[:-1], RUNGS[1:]):\n","        one_rho = 1 - np.corrcoef(rk[l0], rk[l1])[0, 1]\n","        STEPS.append((l1, p1 - p0, one_rho, K_RULE * np.sqrt(one_rho) * 1e5))\n","    one_rho = 1 - np.corrcoef(rankdata(s352), rankdata(s354b))[0, 1]\n","    STEPS_EXTRA = (\"0.10 seed swap vs 0.95352 file\", 2, one_rho, K_RULE * np.sqrt(one_rho) * 1e5)\n","    for s in STEPS: print(f\"  {s[0]:32s} public {s[1]:+3d}e-5   1-rho {s[2]:.2e}   noise SD of the public gap ~{s[3]:.1f}e-5\")\n","    del rk\n","else:\n","    print(\"ladder inputs not all attached; the rung figure uses the OOF moves only\")\n","SIG_RUNG = float(np.median([s[3] for s in STEPS])) if HAVE_LADDER else float(np.median(SD_PUB))\n","log(f\"typical noise of one rung on the public board: {SIG_RUNG:.1f}e-5\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"id":"497454f1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:24:04.131195Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:24:04.130769Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:24:04.443098Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:24:04.442144Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.324954,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:24:04.445169+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:24:04.120215+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  best of  1: public  -1.3e-5   private  -1.5e-5   true (CV)  -1.5e-5\n","  best of  2: public  +1.5e-5   private  -0.9e-5   true (CV)  -0.9e-5\n","  best of  3: public  +2.8e-5   private  -0.9e-5   true (CV)  -0.8e-5\n","  best of  5: public  +4.2e-5   private