" >part of v15</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_46307_row9_col2\" class=\"data row9 col2\" >-7.7</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_46307_row9_col3\" class=\"data row9 col3\" >0/5</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_46307_row9_col4\" class=\"data row9 col4\" >7.9</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_46307_row9_col5\" class=\"data row9 col5\" >80%</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_46307_row9_col6\" class=\"data row9 col6\" >Areeb Ali v15 (with other changes)</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n"],"text/plain":["<pandas.io.formats.style.Styler at 0x7f5c4a7cca50>"]},"execution_count":19,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["rows = []\n","for n, d, pub, src in MOVES:\n","    i = NAMES.index(n)\n","    rows.append({\"probe (step applied to the ladder file)\": n, \"public LB change\": f\"{pub:+d}\",\n","                 \"nested CV change\": f\"{TRUE[n]:+.1f}\", \"folds up\": f\"{UP[n]}/5\",\n","                 \"public noise SD\": f\"{SD_PUB[i]:.1f}\", \"P(public sign = private sign)\": f\"{AGREE[i]:.0%}\", \"source of the public number\": src})\n","i = NAMES.index(\"tree move\")\n","rows.append({\"probe (step applied to the ladder file)\": \"full tree move (-0.10 MLP, -0.05 GB)\", \"public LB change\": \"part of v15\",\n","             \"nested CV change\": f\"{TRUE['tree move']:+.1f}\", \"folds up\": f\"{UP['tree move']}/5\", \"public noise SD\": f\"{SD_PUB[i]:.1f}\",\n","             \"P(public sign = private sign)\": f\"{AGREE[i]:.0%}\", \"source of the public number\": \"Areeb Ali v15 (with other changes)\"})\n","TAB = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n","print(\"All changes in points of 1e-5. Nested CV = applied to the nested OOF of the public wide LM stack (CV %.6f).\" % CV_W)\n","TAB.style.hide(axis=\"index\") if hasattr(TAB.style, \"hide\") else TAB"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":20,"id":"e6dfe903","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.364724Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.363394Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.709722Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.708774Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.365754,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.712822+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.347068+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x616 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(13, 5.6))\n","names_ = [m[0] for m in MOVES] + [\"tree move\"]\n","pubv = [m[2] for m in MOVES] + [np.nan]\n","cvv = [TRUE[n] for n in names_]\n","sdv = [SD_PUB[NAMES.index(n)] for n in names_]\n","yy = np.arange(len(names_))[::-1]\n","for yi, s in zip(yy, sdv):\n","    ax.add_patch(FancyBboxPatch((-s, yi - 0.38), 2 * s, 0.76, boxstyle=\"round,pad=0,rounding_size=0.1\", facecolor=BAND, edgecolor=\"none\", zorder=0))\n","ax.barh(yy + 0.17, pubv, height=0.32, color=PUB, label=\"reported public LB change\", zorder=3)\n","ax.barh(yy - 0.17, cvv, height=0.32, color=[CV if (c > 0 and UP[n] >= 4) else \"#9ccfba\" if c > 0 else PRIV for c, n in zip(cvv, names_)],\n","        label=\"nested CV change\", zorder=3)\n","for yi, n, c in zip(yy, names_, cvv):\n","    ax.text(max(0, c) + 0.4 if c >= 0 else c - 0.4, yi - 0.17, f\"{c:+.1f}  ({UP[n]}/5 folds)\", va=\"center\",\n","            ha=\"left\" if c >= 0 else \"right\", fontsize=8.5, color=INK2)\n","ax.set_yticks(yy); ax.set_yticklabels([SHORT.get(n, \"full tree move\") for n in names_], fontsize=9.5); ax.tick_params(axis=\"y\", length=0)\n","zero_line(ax, \"x\"); ax.xaxis.set_major_formatter(E5); ax.set_xlabel(\"change (x 1e-5)\"); ax.grid(axis=\"y\", visible=False)\n","ax.set_xlim(-17, 8)\n","ax.legend(handles=[Patch(color=PUB, label=\"reported public LB change\"), Patch(color=CV, label=\"nested CV: up on >= 4 of 5 folds\"),\n","                   Patch(color=\"#9ccfba\", label=\"nested CV: up on < 4 folds\"), Patch(color=PRIV, label=\"nested CV: down\"), Patch(color=BAND, label=\"+-1 SD public noise of the step\")],\n","          loc=\"lower left\", fontsize=9)\n","headline(fig, f\"Only the GPT-2 seed swap gains on both boards; {len(POS) - len(CONF)} other public gains are not confirmed by nested CV\",\n","         \"Every public probe that has OOF files behind it, replayed on the nested OOF of the public wide LM stack\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"828f624b","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.016015,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.745172+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.729157+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Reading the table.** The ladder authors saw the same thing and said so: Areeb Ali writes that *\"every earlier ladder\n","step lost on CV\"* and that the two-seed rung is the first one that holds up; goodpjw2008 calls a rung *\"a bet, not a\n","measurement\"*. Our replay agrees with their own CV checks: the two-seed rung gains about +1.9e-5 on 5 of 5 folds\n","(goodpjw2008: +1.9e-5) and the full tree move loses about 7.7e-5 (Areeb Ali: -7.4e-5).\n","\n","The two-seed rung is also the one with a clear mechanism: averaging two seeds of the same model removes part of one\n","seed's noise, which is a gain one expects on any rows. The other steps tune *how much* of a member the file holds, and\n","there the public board and CV disagree; with a public noise SD of 3&ndash;7 points per step, the public board cannot\n","settle a one- or two-point question."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"696d4728","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.015959,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.776821+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.760862+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"s4\"></a>\n","<div style=\"background: #0b1f4b; color: #ffffff; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700;\">4 &middot; The winner's curse</div>\n","\n","Try `K` probes, keep the one with the best public score. Even if none of them is truly better, the best of `K` noisy\n","numbers is above zero, by about `sigma x E[max of K standard normals]`: about 0.8 sigma for K = 3, 1.5 sigma for K = 10,\n","2.0 sigma for K = 30, 2.5 sigma for K = 100. The private part of the same split does not share that luck, so the pick\n","falls back. This is the textbook *winner's curse* (selection bias) and, repeated over many rounds of public feedback,\n","*adaptive overfitting* of the public holdout.\n","\n","Below, the probes are real: small steps from the wide stack towards (or away from) each OOF-bank member and each public\n","LM. On every random split we pick the best of `K` by its public gap and read its private gap."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":21,"id":"8a1f3ad3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.810591Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.809619Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.51856Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.517658Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.730375,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.52292+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:25.792545+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x528 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, (ax, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4.8), gridspec_kw=dict(width_ratios=[1.15, 1]))\n","kk = np.array(KGRID)\n","pub_m = np.array([CURSE[k][:, 0].mean() for k in KGRID]); prv_m = np.array([CURSE[k][:, 1].mean() for k in KGRID])\n","tru_m = np.array([CURSE[k][:, 2].mean() for k in KGRID])\n","ax.fill_between(kk, prv_m, pub_m, color=PUB, alpha=0.08, lw=0)\n","ax.plot(kk, pub_m, \"o-\", color=PUB, ms=7, mec=SURF, label=\"public gap of the pick\")\n","ax.plot(kk, prv_m, \"o-\", color=PRIV, ms=7, mec=SURF, label=\"private gap of the same pick\")\n","ax.plot(kk, tru_m, \"o--\", color=CV, ms=6, mec=SURF, lw=1.4, label=\"nested CV of the pick (its true size)\")\n","ax.annotate(f\"{pub_m[-1] - prv_m[-1]:.1f} points\\nlost on private\", xy=(kk[-1], (pub_m[-1] + prv_m[-1]) / 2), xytext=(-12, 0),\n","            textcoords=\"offset points\", ha=\"right\", va=\"center\", fontsize=9.5, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK)\n","zero_line(ax); ax.set_xscale(\"log\"); ax.set_xticks(KGRID); ax.set_xticklabels([str(k) for k in KGRID])\n","ax.yaxis.set_major_formatter(E5); ax.set_xlabel(\"probes compared on public (K)\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"gap vs. the base file (x 1e-5)\")\n","ax.legend(loc=\"upper left\", fontsize=9)\n","panel_title(ax, \"The more probes you compare, the more the pick is luck\", \"average over random 20/80 splits\")\n","c20 = CURSE[20]\n","ax2.scatter(c20[:, 0], c20[:, 1], s=8, color=PUB, alpha=0.25, edgecolor=\"none\")\n","lim = np.percentile(np.abs(c20[:, :2]), 99.5)\n","ax2.plot([-lim, lim], [-lim, lim], color=MUTED, lw=1, ls=(0, (4, 3)))\n","zero_line(ax2); zero_line(ax2, \"x\"); ax2.set_xlim(-lim, lim); ax2.set_ylim(-lim, lim)\n","ax2.xaxis.set_major_formatter(E5); ax2.yaxis.set_major_formatter(E5)\n","ax2.set_xlabel(\"public gap of the best of 20 (x 1e-5)\"); ax2.set_ylabel(\"its private gap (x 1e-5)\")\n","ax2.text(0.97, 0.05, f\"public > 0 in {np.mean(c20[:, 0] > 0):.0%} of splits\\nprivate > 0 in {np.mean(c20[:, 1] > 0):.0%}\",\n","         transform=ax2.transAxes, ha=\"right\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=9.5, color=INK)\n","panel_title(ax2, \"Best of 20: almost always up on public\", \"each dot = one random split\")\n","headline(fig, \"Keeping the best public probe buys public points that the private board does not pay\",\n","         \"Real probes on the public wide-stack OOF; public and private parts drawn independently in each split\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1f08acb5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.017141,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.557749+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.540608+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<div style=\"background: #fff4ec; border-left: 5px solid #eb6834; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 6px 0;\">\n","<b>How many probes are behind a public file?</b> The version tables list ten versions for one ladder (v9&ndash;v20) and\n","about twenty scored probes for the other, and these ladders build on each other. On the leaderboard snapshot the\n","median top-50 team had made about 20 submissions on 12 Nov (28 on 14 Nov), and the top teams over 100. With a rung noise of a few points,\n","the theory says the best of 20 null probes shows about 1.9 noise SDs of public \"gain\". That is the size of the whole\n","visible spread between many of the top files.\n","</div>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3cd84db6","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.017153,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.592167+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.575014+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"s5\"></a>\n","<div style=\"background: #0b1f4b; color: #ffffff; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700;\">5 &middot; CV can be tuned too</div>\n","\n","Nested CV is the referee in this notebook, so it is fair to ask how a CV number can itself be inflated. Three common\n","ways, each measured below on public data:\n","\n","1. **Early stopping on the scored fold.** The fold that reports the score also picks the number of trees.\n","2. **Selecting on the reported folds.** A blend, a member set or a weight chosen on the same OOF rows it is scored on.\n","3. **A test inside one fold.** An inner CV run on the rows of a single outer fold measures something else."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":22,"id":"237fa405","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.629883Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.628799Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:29:40.512096Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:29:40.511065Z"},"papermill":{"duration":133.921782,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:29:40.531499+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:27:26.609717+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[ 8.5 min] fold 0: trees picked on scored fold 520 (AUC 0.945106), on inner 10% 1260 (scored AUC 0.944626) -> optimism +48.0e-5\n","[ 9.2 min] fold 1: trees picked on scored fold 1190 (AUC 0.948970), on inner 10% 850 (scored AUC 0.948802) -> optimism +16.8e-5\n","[10.0 min] fold 2: trees picked on scored fold 670 (AUC 0.951211), on inner 10% 310 (scored AUC 0.950652) -> optimism +55.9e-5\n"]}],"source":["# 5.1  Early stopping on the scored fold: one 4-leaf LightGBM per outer fold on the raw columns (learning rate 0.1),\n","# trained on 90% of the training part. We record the AUC every 10 trees on the scored fold AND on the held-out 10%,\n","# so the two ways of choosing the number of trees are compared on the very same model.\n","import lightgbm as lgb\n","NTH = int(os.environ.get(\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\", 4))\n","X = train.drop(columns=[\"id\", \"is_fraud\"]).copy()\n","for c in X.columns:\n","    if X[c].dtype == object: X[c] = X[c].astype(\"category\")\n","    elif X[c].dtype == bool: X[c] = X[c].astype(int)\n","ES_FOLDS, ES_ROUNDS, STEP = [0, 1, 2], 1500, 10\n","ES = []\n","for k in ES_FOLDS:\n","    va = FOLDS[k]; tr = np.setdiff1d(np.arange(N), va)\n","    inner = np.random.default_rng(k).random(len(tr)) < 0.10\n","    a, h = tr[~inner], tr[inner]\n","    bst = lgb.train(dict(objective=\"binary\", num_leaves=4, learning_rate=0.1, min_data_in_leaf=100, verbose=-1,\n","                         num_threads=NTH, seed=k), lgb.Dataset(X.iloc[a], y[a]), num_boost_round=ES_ROUNDS)\n","    zh, zv = np.zeros(len(h)), np.zeros(len(va)); its, ah, av = [], [], []\n","    for s in range(0, ES_ROUNDS, STEP):\n","        zh += bst.predict(X.iloc[h], start_iteration=s, num_iteration=STEP, raw_score=True)\n","        zv += bst.predict(X.iloc[va], start_iteration=s, num_iteration=STEP, raw_score=True)\n","        its.append(s + STEP); ah.append(roc_auc_score(y[h], zh)); av.append(roc_auc_score(y[va], zv))\n","    its, ah, av = map(np.array, (its, ah, av))\n","    i_sc, i_in = av.argmax(), ah.argmax()\n","    ES.append(dict(fold=k, its=its, av=av, i_sc=i_sc, i_in=i_in, opt=(av[i_sc] - av[i_in]) * 1e5))\n","    log(f\"fold {k}: trees picked on scored fold {its[i_sc]} (AUC {av[i_sc]:.6f}), on inner 10% {its[i_in]} \"\n","        f\"(scored AUC {av[i_in]:.6f}) -> optimism {ES[-1]['opt']:+.1f}e-5\")\n","del X"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":23,"id":"cd0f2df3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:29:40.568257Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:29:40.56781Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:29:40.990468Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:29:40.989457Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.445321,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:29:40.994162+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:29:40.548841+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x506 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, (ax, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4.6), gridspec_kw=dict(width_ratios=[1.7, 1]))\n","FC = [C[0], C[6], C[3]]\n","for e, col in zip(ES, FC):\n","    rel = (e[\"av\"] - e[\"av\"][e[\"i_sc\"]]) * 1e5\n","    ax.plot(e[\"its\"], rel, color=col, lw=1.6, label=f\"fold {e['fold']}\")\n","    ax.plot(e[\"its\"][e[\"i_sc\"]], 0, \"o\", ms=8, color=col, mec=SURF, mew=1.5, zorder=5)\n","    ax.plot(e[\"its\"][e[\"i_in\"]], rel[e[\"i_in\"]], \"D\", ms=7, mfc=SURF, mec=col, mew=1.8, zorder=5)\n","low = min((e[\"av\"][e[\"i_in\"]] - e[\"av\"][e[\"i_sc\"]]) * 1e5 for e in ES)\n","ax.set_ylim(low * 1.6 - 5, 8); ax.set_xlim(100, ES_ROUNDS); ax.yaxis.set_major_formatter(E5)\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"number of trees\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"scored-fold AUC minus its maximum (x 1e-5)\")\n","ax.legend(handles=[Line2D([], [], color=c, lw=2, label=f\"fold {e['fold']}\") for e, c in zip(ES, FC)] +\n","          [Line2D([], [], marker=\"o\", ls=\"\", color=INK2, label=\"trees chosen on the scored fold\"),\n","           Line2D([], [], marker=\"D\", ls=\"\", mfc=SURF, mec=INK2, label=\"trees chosen on a held-out 10%\")], loc=\"lower right\", fontsize=8.5)\n","panel_title(ax, \"The top of a noisy curve is always the highest point\", \"scored-fold AUC along training, 4-leaf LightGBM, learning rate 0.1\")\n","opts = [e[\"opt\"] for e in ES]\n","ax2.bar(range(len(ES)), opts, color=PRIV, width=0.55)\n","for i, v in enumerate(opts): ax2.text(i, v + 0.3, f\"+{v:.1f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=10, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK)\n","ax2.set_xticks(range(len(ES))); ax2.set_xticklabels([f\"fold {e['fold']}\" for e in ES]); ax2.yaxis.set_major_formatter(E5)\n","ax2.set_ylabel(\"optimism of the reported fold AUC (x 1e-5)\"); ax2.set_ylim(0, max(opts) * 1.3 + 1)\n","panel_title(ax2, f\"Free optimism: {np.mean(opts):+.1f}e-5 per fold\", \"scored-fold pick minus held-out pick\")\n","headline(fig, f\"Early stopping on the scored fold reports {np.mean(opts):.0f} points more than an honest choice of trees\",\n","         \"Same model, two ways to choose the number of trees: on the fold that is scored, or on a held-out 10% of the training part\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a94010cd","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.020049,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:29:41.034939+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:29:41.01489+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["The held-out 10% is itself a noisy judge, so its pick lands away from the scored-fold peak: that is the point. The\n","scored-fold pick hides this noise and reports the peak; any choice made without the scored rows pays for it.\n","A fast learner (learning rate 0.1) is the bad case: its curve is jagged, so the maximum of the scored fold sits well\n","above what a choice made elsewhere achieves. With the slower learning rate most public tree members use (0.03) a\n","separate measurement of the same comparison gave about **+2 to +3e-5 per member**. Per member that is small next to\n","fold noise, but it is **systematic**: a stack of a hundred members\n","that all stopped on their scored fold inherits it, and stack weights then favour the members whose OOF is most\n","optimistic. Choosing the number of trees on a held-out slice of the training part\n","costs nothing and removes it."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":24,"id":"b1e05fb0","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:29:41.076046Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:29:41.075638Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:31:50.468097Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:31:50.467046Z"},"papermill":{"duration":129.415649,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:50.470129+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:29:41.05448+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[10.7 min]   hill climbing, outer fold 0: picks ['gb_bag10', 'gbn_bag5_w128', 'lgb_dig_l7', 'gb_bag10'] ...\n","[11.1 min]   hill climbing, outer fold 1: picks ['gb_bag10', 'gb_bag10', 'gb_bag10', 'lgb_dig_l7'] ...\n","[11.4 min]   hill climbing, outer fold 2: picks ['gb_bag10', 'gb_bag10', 'lgb_dig_s100_bag5', 'gbn_bag5_w128'] ...\n","[11.7 min]   hill climbing, outer fold 3: picks ['gb_bag10', 'gbn_bag5_w512', 'lgb_diglead_l3_bag', 'gbx_bag5'] ...\n","[12.1 min]   hill climbing, outer fold 4: picks ['gb_bag10', 'lgb_dig_l7', 'gb_bag10', 'gbn_bag5_w128'] ...\n","[12.1 min] hill climbing: reported (non-nested) CV 0.951656, nested CV 0.951541, gap +11.5e-5\n"]}],"source":["# 5.2  Selecting on the reported folds: greedy hill climbing (Caruana) over the OOF bank's 20 core members.\n","# Non-nested: choose the blend on all OOF rows, report its CV on the same rows.  Nested: choose on 4 folds, score the 5th.\n","names = list(BANK); M = np.stack([BANK[n] for n in names], 1).astype(np.float32)\n","HC_STEPS = 10\n","def hill_climb(rows):\n","    \"\"\"Greedy forward selection with replacement on `rows`; returns the list of picks (indices into names).\"\"\"\n","    yr = y[rows]; Mr = M[rows]\n","    first = int(np.argmax([auc_sort(yr, Mr[:, j]) for j in range(M.shape[1])]))\n","    picks, s = [first], Mr[:, first].astype(np.float64).copy()\n","    for _ in range(HC_STEPS - 1):\n","        sc = [auc_sort(yr, s + Mr[:, j]) for j in range(M.shape[1])]\n","        j = int(np.argmax(sc)); picks.append(j); s += Mr[:, j]\n","    return picks\n","def blend(picks, upto): return M[:, picks[:upto]].mean(1)\n","full_picks = hill_climb(np.arange(N))\n","HC_NON = [cv(blend(full_picks, t)) for t in range(1, HC_STEPS + 1)]\n","HC_NEST = np.zeros((5, HC_STEPS))\n","for k, b in enumerate(FOLDS):\n","    p = hill_climb(np.setdiff1d(np.arange(N), b))\n","    for t in range(1, HC_STEPS + 1): HC_NEST[k, t - 1] = roc_auc_score(y[b], blend(p, t)[b])\n","    log(f\"  hill climbing, outer fold {k}: picks {[names[j] for j in p[:4]]} ...\")\n","HC_NEST_CV = HC_NEST.mean(0)\n","BEST_SINGLE = max(cv(M[:, j]) for j in range(M.shape[1]))\n","log(f\"hill climbing: reported (non-nested) CV {HC_NON[-1]:.6f}, nested CV {HC_NEST_CV[-1]:.6f}, gap {(HC_NON[-1] - HC_NEST_CV[-1]) * 1e5:+.1f}e-5\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":25,"id":"b2fa2b7e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:31:50.510554Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:31:50.5101Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:31:58.801961Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:31:58.801287Z"},"papermill":{"duration":8.315312,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:58.80448+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:50.489168+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  fold 0: inner test  +11.9e-5   outer test  -12.9e-5\n","  fold 1: inner test   -8.1e-5   outer test   +0.1e-5\n","  fold 2: inner test   -4.6e-5   outer test   +0.8e-5\n","  fold 3: inner test   -5.5e-5   outer test   -1.6e-5\n","  fold 4: inner test   -3.7e-5   outer test   -0.5e-5\n"]}],"source":["# 5.3  A test inside one fold: does adding megayak's LM (already a member of the wide stack) to W help?\n","# Outer test: weights fitted on the other four folds, scored on fold k.  Inner test: a 5-fold CV inside fold k's rows only.\n","Z = np.c_[W, O[\"LM\"]]\n","INOUT = []\n","for k, b in enumerate(FOLDS):\n","    rest = np.setdiff1d(np.arange(N), b)\n","    lr_ = LogisticRegression(C=1.0, max_iter=500).fit(Z[rest], y[rest])\n","    outer = roc_auc_score(y[b], Z[b] @ lr_.coef_[0]) - roc_auc_score(y[b], W[b])\n","    ins = []\n","    for it, ib in StratifiedKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=0).split(b, y[b]):\n","        l2 = LogisticRegression(C=1.0, max_iter=500).fit(Z[b[it]], y[b[it]])\n","        ins.append(roc_auc_score(y[b[ib]], Z[b[ib]] @ l2.coef_[0]) - roc_auc_score(y[b[ib]], W[b[ib]]))\n","    INOUT.append((k, np.mean(ins) * 1e5, outer * 1e5))\n","    print(f\"  fold {k}: inner test {np.mean(ins) * 1e5:+6.1f}e-5   outer test {outer * 1e5:+6.1f}e-5\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":26,"id":"a5ea051e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:31:58.873279Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:31:58.872922Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.358858Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.357905Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.52413,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.362315+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:58.838185+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x528 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, (ax, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4.8), gridspec_kw=dict(width_ratios=[1.25, 1]))\n","t = np.arange(1, HC_STEPS + 1)\n","ax.plot(t, (np.array(HC_NON) - BEST_SINGLE) * 1e5, color=PRIV, marker=\"o\", ms=6, mec=SURF, label=\"reported: chosen and scored on the same OOF\")\n","ax.plot(t, (HC_NEST_CV - BEST_SINGLE) * 1e5, color=CV, marker=\"o\", ms=6, mec=SURF, label=\"nested: chosen on 4 folds, scored on the 5th\")\n","gap = (HC_NON[-1] - HC_NEST_CV[-1]) * 1e5\n","ax.annotate(f\"gap {gap:+.1f}e-5\", xy=(HC_STEPS, (HC_NON[-1] - BEST_SINGLE) * 1e5), xytext=(-8, 14), textcoords=\"offset points\",\n","            ha=\"right\", fontsize=10, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK)\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"hill-climbing step (members in the blend, with repeats)\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"CV gain over the best single member (x 1e-5)\")\n","ax.yaxis.set_major_formatter(E5); ax.set_xticks(t); ax.legend(loc=\"lower right\", fontsize=9)\n","panel_title(ax, f\"Selection on the scored rows reads {gap:.0f} points high\", \"greedy blend of the OOF bank's 20 core members\")\n","ks = [r[0] for r in INOUT]\n","for k, i_, o_ in INOUT:\n","    ax2.plot([i_, o_], [k, k], color=RULE, lw=3, zorder=1)\n","ax2.scatter([r[1] for r in INOUT], ks, s=70, color=PRIV, zorder=3, label=\"inner CV inside the fold\", edgecolor=SURF, lw=1.5)\n","ax2.scatter([r[2] for r in INOUT], ks, s=70, color=CV, zorder=3, label=\"outer test on the fold\", edgecolor=SURF, lw=1.5)\n","zero_line(ax2, \"x\"); ax2.set_yticks(ks); ax2.set_yticklabels([f\"fold {k}\" for k in ks]); ax2.invert_yaxis()\n","ax2.xaxis.set_major_formatter(E5); ax2.set_xlabel(\"gain from adding a member already in the stack (x 1e-5)\")\n","ax2.legend(loc=\"lower right\", fontsize=9)\n","n_dis = sum(np.sign(i_) != np.sign(o_) for _, i_, o_ in INOUT)\n","panel_title(ax2, f\"Inner and outer verdicts disagree on {n_dis} of 5 folds\", \"logistic re-weighting of the wide stack + megayak LM\")\n","headline(fig, \"Where you select and where you score must be different rows\",\n","         \"Left: a blend picked on the OOF it is scored on. Right: a decision taken inside one fold versus across folds.\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d31ba851","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.021719,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.405186+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.383467+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<div style=\"background: #fff4ec; border-left: 5px solid #eb6834; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 6px 0;\">\n","<b>Rules of thumb for an honest CV.</b> (1) Stop trees on a held-out slice of the training part, never on the scored\n","fold. (2) Every choice a pipeline makes (members, weights, C, gates, transforms) is made inside the training part of\n","each outer fold: that is <i>nested</i> CV. (3) Decide across all outer folds, not inside one: a fold-local test sees\n","that fold's own calibration and noise. (4) A stack fitted once on the full OOF and then reported on the same OOF reads\n","high; fit it again fold by fold to get the number you can compare.\n","</div>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"539e9d1e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.020601,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.448033+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.427432+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"s6\"></a>\n","<div style=\"background: #0b1f4b; color: #ffffff; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700;\">6 &middot; What did not work</div>\n","\n","Negative results are rarely published and save everyone time. First, public probes that the ladder authors reported\n","as losses (all credit to them for publishing these):\n","\n","| probe on a ladder file | public change | reported by |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| + 0.12 of the public target-first GPT-2 (already inside every ladder file) | -14 | goodpjw2008 (v1 probes) |\n","| + 5% / + 2% TabPFN-3.5 | -1 / -1 | Areeb Ali (v18 and probes) |\n","| 10% mix with another public stack | -1 | Areeb Ali |\n","| + 10% / + 20% of a GPT-2 + GLM fusion file | 0 / 0 | Areeb Ali |\n","| more of both LMs (+0.04, +0.03) | -2 | Areeb Ali |\n","| an extra LM step on daoviet's file, other LM kept at 0.12 | 0 | goodpjw2008 |\n","\n","Areeb Ali's summary: *\"new model families (TabPFN, GBDT files, other stacks) lose a point\"*. On nested CV, adding more\n","language-model weight to a wide stack also loses (-2.8e-5, up on only 2 of 5 folds in our check), even though public\n","ladders gained points from LM steps.\n","\n","Second, \"smarter\" ways to combine a bank of public OOF predictions, each compared on **nested CV over 5 outer folds**\n","with every setting fixed in advance, against simply keeping a strong logistic stack:\n","\n","| method | nested CV vs. the plain stack | folds better |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| greedy hill climbing (Caruana), bank that already contains the stack | +0.0 (it picks the stack alone) | 0/5 |\n","| logistic regression on all ~80 deduplicated members, C by inner CV | -27.7e-5 | 0/5 |\n","| weights proportional to pairwise AUC | -40.6e-5 | 0/5 |\n","| two experts gated by a data segment | -30.9e-5 | 0/5 |\n","| stack + a small segment-gate correction | -1.9e-5 | 0/5 |\n","| non-linear meta-model (4-leaf LightGBM on members, member disagreement, raw columns) | -39e-5 to -56e-5 | 0&ndash;1/5 |\n","\n","<div style=\"background: #eefaf4; border-left: 5px solid #1baf7a; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 6px 0;\">\n","<b>Pattern.</b> Once a linear stack holds the strong members, cleverer combiners mostly fit noise: they lose on\n","every outer fold by far more than any ladder step gains. The one kind of change that kept gaining on nested CV in the\n","public record is <b>new information</b> (another seed or another view of a strong model), not new weights.\n","</div>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b853314f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.021811,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.490437+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.468626+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"s7\"></a>\n","<div style=\"background: #0b1f4b; color: #ffffff; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700;\">7 &middot; What to expect on private, and how to pick two final files</div>\n","\n","Put the pieces together for the current public top file. We replay its checkable steps on the nested OOF, in the\n","order they were built, and set them beside the public points each one earned."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":27,"id":"933a2c18","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.535268Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.534751Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:32:01.912964Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:32:01.912016Z"},"papermill":{"duration":2.403042,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:01.91527+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:31:59.512228+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  Strike 9 -> Strike 10        public +10   nested CV   no OOF\n","  + 0.6 (S10 - S9)             public  +2   nested CV   no OOF\n","  + 0.12 megayak LM            public  +1   nested CV  -4.9  (1/5 folds up)\n","  -> 0.95352 file (4 steps)    public  +9   nested CV  -4.9  (1/5 folds up)\n","  + GPT-2 seed swap            public  +2   nested CV  +1.6  (4/5 folds up)\n","checkable steps: public +12 points, nested CV -8.2 points\n"]}],"source":["D_a3 = 0.12 * (O[\"LM\"] - W)\n","D_352 = 0.09 * (O[\"LM\"] - W) + 0.09 * (O[\"L7F\"] - W) + 0.05 * (O[\"GPD\"] - W) - 0.05 * (O[\"MLP\"] - W) - 0.025 * (O[\"GB\"] - W)\n","c_a3, c_352 = W + D_a3, W + D_352\n","c_354 = L(c_352) + 0.06 * (O[\"G26\"] - O[\"MS\"])\n","CHAIN = [(\"Strike 9 -> Strike 10\", 10, None, None), (\"+ 0.6 (S10 - S9)\", 2, None, None),\n","         (\"+ 0.12 megayak LM\", 1, (cv(c_a3) - CV_W) * 1e5, folds_up(c_a3, W)),\n","         (\"-> 0.95352 file\\n(4 steps)\", 9, (cv(c_352) - cv(c_a3)) * 1e5, folds_up(c_352, c_a3)),\n","         (\"+ GPT-2 seed swap\", 2, (cv(c_354) - cv(c_352)) * 1e5, folds_up(c_354, c_352))]\n","CHECK_PUB = sum(c[1] for c in CHAIN if c[2] is not None); CHECK_CV = sum(c[2] for c in CHAIN if c[2] is not None)\n","for lab, p, c, u in CHAIN:\n","    print(f\"  {lab.replace(chr(10), ' '):28s} public {p:+3d}   nested CV \" + (\"  no OOF\" if c is None else f\"{c:+5.1f}  ({u}/5 folds up)\"))\n","print(f\"checkable steps: public {CHECK_PUB:+d} points, nested CV {CHECK_CV:+.1f} points\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":28,"id":"ba7ec6cc","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:32:01.959697Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:32:01.959231Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.222708Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.221802Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.289334,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.225687+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:01.936353+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x550 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(13, 5.0))\n","x = np.arange(len(CHAIN))\n","ax.bar(x - 0.2, [c[1] for c in CHAIN], width=0.38, color=PUB, label=\"public LB points earned\")\n","for i, (lab, p, c, u) in enumerate(CHAIN):\n","    ax.text(i - 0.2, p + 0.3, f\"+{p}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=10, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK)\n","    if c is None:\n","        ax.bar(i + 0.2, 4, width=0.38, color=\"none\", edgecolor=MUTED, hatch=\"///\", lw=0)\n","        ax.text(i + 0.2, 4.3, \"no OOF:\\nuntestable\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=8.5, color=INK2)\n","    else:\n","        ax.bar(i + 0.2, c, width=0.38, color=CV if (c > 0 and u >= 4) else PRIV)\n","        ax.text(i + 0.2, c + (0.3 if c >= 0 else -0.3), f\"{c:+.1f}\\n({u}/5)\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\" if c >= 0 else \"top\", fontsize=9, color=INK)\n","zero_line(ax); ax.set_xticks(x); ax.set_xticklabels([c[0] for c in CHAIN], fontsize=9.5); ax.yaxis.set_major_formatter(E5)\n","ax.set_ylabel(\"points (x 1e-5)\"); ax.grid(axis=\"x\", visible=False)\n","ax.set_ylim(min(-8, min(c[2] for c in CHAIN if c[2] is not None) - 3), 14)\n","ax.legend(handles=[Patch(color=PUB, label=\"public LB points earned\"), Patch(color=CV, label=\"nested CV: confirmed\"),\n","                   Patch(color=PRIV, label=\"nested CV: not confirmed\"), Patch(facecolor=\"none\", edgecolor=MUTED, hatch=\"///\", label=\"no OOF published\")],\n","          loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=9)\n","headline(fig, f\"Of the +24 public points from Strike 9 to the top file, the checkable +{CHECK_PUB} are worth {CHECK_CV:+.1f} on nested CV\",\n","         \"Each step of the 0.95354 ladder file replayed on the nested OOF of the public wide LM stack (moves applied in the same order)\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"13fa4dad","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.024209,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.272198+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.247989+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What this means for the private board** (an estimate, not a forecast):\n","\n","* The absolute private score of every file can sit a few *thousandths* away from its public score, in the same\n","  direction for everyone. Nobody can know that direction; it does not change the ranking.\n","* The **ranking** inside the top band depends on gaps of a few points, and each gap carries a public noise of about\n","  one ladder-rung SD. Expect the top of the private board to reshuffle by that much.\n","* Steps that nested CV did not confirm have an expected private value near their CV value, not their public value.\n","  Steps without any OOF (the base files and the extrapolation) are a genuine unknown: they may hold, or not.\n","* The two-seed rung is the exception that proves the method: it won on both boards and has a mechanism.\n","\n","<div style=\"background: #eefaf4; border-left: 5px solid #1baf7a; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 6px 0;\">\n","<b>Picking two final files &mdash; general advice.</b><br>\n","<b>1. One CV-backed file.</b> Every choice in it (members, weights, early stopping) made inside the training folds; its\n","nested CV is the number you trust. Its public score may sit below the ladders; that is fine.<br>\n","<b>2. One different hypothesis.</b> If you believe a public ladder's untestable base carries real signal, that is a\n","legitimate second pick &mdash; but make the second file genuinely <i>different</i> from the first (lower rank\n","correlation), so the two picks hedge each other.<br>\n","<b>3. Never two near-copies.</b> Two files at rank correlation 0.9999 land within a few points of each other on\n","private: the second slot is wasted.<br>\n","<b>4. Do not let the public board choose between close files.</b> If two candidates differ by less than about two\n","noise SDs (use <code>public_gap_noise()</code> above), the public board cannot tell them apart; decide by CV or by\n","reasoning.\n","</div>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ecb1c029","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.023202,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.319425+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.296223+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"s8\"></a>\n","<div style=\"background: #0b1f4b; color: #ffffff; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700;\">8 &middot; New in v4: the board, 12 &rarr; 14 November</div>\n","\n","In two days the band moved up by about three hundred-thousandths and two new public notebooks took the top of the\n","Code list. The leaderboard snapshot below is from 14 Nov, 01:03 UTC (scores and submission counts only)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":29,"id":"ec43fed4","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.365954Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.365236Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.97053Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.969656Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.632329,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.973846+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.341517+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x550 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, (ax, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 5.0), gridspec_kw=dict(width_ratios=[1.25, 1]))\n","rk12, rk14 = np.arange(1, len(LB_TOP) + 1), np.arange(1, len(LB14_TOP) + 1)\n","ax.plot(rk12, LB_TOP, color=MUTED, lw=2, label=\"12 Nov, 12:11 UTC\")\n","ax.plot(rk14, LB14_TOP, color=PUB, lw=2.2, label=\"14 Nov, 01:03 UTC\")\n","for v in (354, 370, 388): ax.axhline(v, color=RULE, lw=1, zorder=0)\n","ax.text(330, 520, \"thin lines, top to bottom: public notebook files\\n0.95388 Bold, Then Bolder  ·  0.95370 rank-1 q17 file\\n0.95354 two-seed ladders (the v3 top)\",\n","        fontsize=8.5, color=INK2, ha=\"right\", va=\"bottom\")\n","for i, lab in [(0, \"#1\"), (1, \"#2\")]:\n","    ax.annotate(f\"{lab}  0.95{LB14_TOP[i]:03d}\", (rk14[i], LB14_TOP[i]), xytext=(14, -4), textcoords=\"offset points\", fontsize=9,\n","                fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK, va=\"center\")\n","ax.set_xscale(\"log\"); ax.set_xlim(0.8, 340); ax.set_ylim(300, 800)\n","ax.set_xticks([1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 300]); ax.set_xticklabels([\"1\", \"2\", \"5\", \"10\", \"20\", \"50\", \"100\", \"300\"])\n","ax.yaxis.set_major_formatter(FuncFormatter(lambda v, _: f\"0.95{int(v):03d}\"))\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"leaderboard rank\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"public LB score\"); ax.legend(loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=9)\n","panel_title(ax, \"The band rose; two scores sit far above it\", \"public score at every rank, both snapshots\")\n","# panel B: where #1 sits, in noise SDs of the gap between two DIFFERENT strong files\n","gaps = (LB14_TOP[:12] - BAND14) / FAR_SD\n","cols = [PRIV if g > 2 else PUB for g in gaps]\n","ax2.bar(np.arange(1, 13), gaps, color=cols, width=0.68, zorder=3)\n","ax2.axhspan(-2, 2, color=BAND, zorder=0, lw=0)\n","ax2.text(12.4, 1.7, \"within 2 noise SDs of #5\", ha=\"right\", va=\"top\", fontsize=8.5, color=INK2)\n","for i, g in enumerate(gaps[:3]):\n","    ax2.text(i + 1, g + 0.15, f\"{g:.1f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=9.5, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK)\n","zero_line(ax2); ax2.set_xticks(np.arange(1, 13)); ax2.set_xlabel(\"leaderboard rank (14 Nov)\")\n","ax2.set_ylabel(\"score minus #5, in noise SDs\"); ax2.grid(axis=\"x\", visible=False); ax2.set_ylim(-1.0, gaps[0] * 1.15)\n","panel_title(ax2, f\"#1 is {gaps[0]:.1f} noise SDs above #5\", f\"1 SD = {FAR_SD:.0f} points: public gap noise of two different strong files (rho {FAR_RHO:.3f})\")\n","headline(fig, f\"In two days the band rose ~{LB14_TOP[49] - LB_TOP[49]} points at #50; #1 at 0.95{LB14_TOP[0]} is far outside any public-noise range\",\n","         f\"Leaderboard snapshots 12 Nov ({LB_TEAMS:,} teams) and 14 Nov ({LB14_TEAMS:,} teams); noise from random 20/80 splits of the public wide-stack OOF\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a9b9eca0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.02469,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:03.023227+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:02.998537+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**How to read panel B.** The noise SD used here is the *largest* one in this notebook: the public gap between two\n","genuinely different strong files (the wide LM stack and the best of mathsonchain's single models, rank correlation\n","about 0.987), measured on random 20/80 splits. Gaps between ladder files are ten times less noisy. Even on this\n","generous scale, #1 is many SDs above the band, so public noise does not explain it; nothing else about that entry is\n","known from public data, and this notebook makes no claim about it. #2 is also well above the band. From #5 down, the\n","board is again a dense band in which neighbours are well inside each other's noise."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"992f1f0c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.02573,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:03.074313+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:03.048583+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"s9\"></a>\n","<div style=\"background: #0b1f4b; color: #ffffff; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700;\">9 &middot; New in v4: anatomy of the two new ladders</div>\n","\n","Both new top notebooks publish every probe with its public score and an OOF check of each mix, which is what makes\n","the replay below possible. Thank you to **goodpjw2008** and **Areeb Ali** again, and to **Aman Atar** for the bundle\n","both are built on.\n","\n","* **goodpjw2008, [LM Ladder | Public and CV Up | LB 0.95386](https://www.kaggle.com/code/goodpjw2008/s6e11-lm-ladder-public-and-cv-up-lb-0-95386).**\n","  Starts from Aman Atar's public 0.95370 file (with 0.06 of one LM moved to the other) and moves it towards 87 public\n","  members. The weights maximise *OOF change + mu x a forecast of the public change*, where the forecast is a model\n","  fitted on 44 of the author's own scored files (not shipped). Three settings were submitted: careful 0.95376,\n","  balanced 0.95380, **bold 0.95386**.\n","* **Areeb Ali, [Bold, Then Bolder | LB 0.95388](https://www.kaggle.com/code/areebbb/s6e11-bold-then-bolder-lb-0-95388).**\n","  Rebuilds the three mixes byte for byte and probes eight steps beyond bold on the board. Keeps\n","  **bold + 0.5 (bold - balanced) = 0.95388**.\n","\n","```\n","U0    = rank(AT + 0.06 (LM7 - LM))                         # AT = the public 0.95370 file (Aman Atar)\n","mix   = (1 - sum_k w_k) logit(U0) + sum_k w_k member_k      # 87 members, logit ranks\n","w     = w_bold + 0.5 (w_bold - w_balanced)                  # 0.95388\n","```\n","\n","Every mix is linear in its weights, so every probe of both notebooks can be rebuilt on the test rows (for its noise)\n","and on the OOF rows (for its CV) from the same public inputs. The base file has no OOF of its own; its OOF stand-in is\n","goodpjw2008's replay of it from the 16 bundle models and the wide LM stack (R&sup2; shown in the log above)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":30,"id":"2e075ea8","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:32:03.12676Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:32:03.126156Z","iop