e rule of section 2).\")\n","show9.style.hide(axis=\"index\") if hasattr(show9.style, \"hide\") else show9"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":31,"id":"8163e22c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:32:04.596174Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:32:04.595326Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.049486Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.047931Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.486991,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.053704+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:04.566713+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x792 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(13, 7.2))\n","yy = np.arange(len(T9))[::-1]\n","for yi, r in zip(yy, T9.itertuples()):\n","    ax.add_patch(FancyBboxPatch((-2 * r.sd, yi - 0.36), 4 * r.sd, 0.72, boxstyle=\"round,pad=0,rounding_size=0.1\", facecolor=BAND, edgecolor=\"none\", zorder=0))\n","    ax.add_patch(FancyBboxPatch((-r.sd, yi - 0.36), 2 * r.sd, 0.72, boxstyle=\"round,pad=0,rounding_size=0.1\", facecolor=RULE, edgecolor=\"none\", zorder=0))\n","    ax.plot(r.pub, yi + 0.13, \"o\", ms=9, color=PUB, mec=SURF, mew=1.4, zorder=4)\n","    if not np.isnan(r.cv):\n","        ax.plot(r.cv, yi - 0.13, \"D\", ms=7.5, color=CV if (r.up >= 4 and r.cv > 0) else PRIV if r.cv < 0 else MUTED, mec=SURF, mew=1.2, zorder=4)\n","        ax.text(max(r.cv, r.pub, 2 * r.sd) + 1.2, yi, f\"OOF {r.cv:+.1f} ({int(r.up)}/5 folds up)\", va=\"center\", fontsize=8.5, color=INK2)\n","    else:\n","        ax.text(max(r.pub, 2 * r.sd) + 1.2, yi, \"no OOF: untestable\", va=\"center\", fontsize=8.5, color=MUTED)\n","    if not np.isnan(r.nested): ax.plot(r.nested, yi - 0.13, \"D\", ms=7.5, mfc=SURF, mec=CVTXT, mew=1.6, zorder=5)\n","ax.axhline(len(T9) - 4.5, color=RULE, lw=1); ax.axhline(len(T9) - 1.5, color=RULE, lw=1)\n","ax.text(-38, len(T9) - 1.0, \"base switch\", fontsize=8.5, color=MUTED, va=\"center\")\n","ax.text(-38, len(T9) - 3.0, \"goodpjw2008:\\nthree mixes vs\\nthe 0.95370 file\", fontsize=8.5, color=MUTED, va=\"center\")\n","ax.text(-38, 3.5, \"Areeb Ali:\\neight probes\\nvs the bold mix\", fontsize=8.5, color=MUTED, va=\"center\")\n","ax.set_yticks(yy); ax.set_yticklabels(T9.step, fontsize=9); ax.tick_params(axis=\"y\", length=0)\n","zero_line(ax, \"x\"); ax.xaxis.set_major_formatter(E5); ax.set_xlim(-40, 62); ax.grid(axis=\"y\", visible=False)\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"change vs the file the step was built on (x 1e-5)\")\n","ax.legend(handles=[Line2D([], [], marker=\"o\", ls=\"\", color=PUB, ms=8, label=\"public LB change\"),\n","                   Line2D([], [], marker=\"D\", ls=\"\", color=CV, ms=7, label=\"OOF change, up on >= 4 of 5 folds\"),\n","                   Line2D([], [], marker=\"D\", ls=\"\", color=MUTED, ms=7, label=\"OOF change, fewer folds up\"),\n","                   Line2D([], [], marker=\"D\", ls=\"\", color=PRIV, ms=7, label=\"OOF change < 0\"),\n","                   Line2D([], [], marker=\"D\", ls=\"\", mfc=SURF, mec=CVTXT, mew=1.6, ms=7, label=\"authors' nested CV\"),\n","                   Patch(color=RULE, label=\"1 SD public noise\"), Patch(color=BAND, label=\"2 SD\")],\n","          loc=\"upper center\", bbox_to_anchor=(0.45, -0.11), ncol=4, fontsize=8.5)\n","_k = T9[T9.step == \"bold + 0.5 (bold - balanced) (kept)\"].iloc[0]\n","headline(fig, f\"The new ladders: the mixes are big moves with OOF behind them; the kept last step is {_k.pub / _k.sd:.1f} noise SD\",\n","         \"Every public probe of both notebooks, rebuilt from public files: public change, its noise, and the OOF change of the same move\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"83c5b2e3","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.026503,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.106997+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.080494+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What the anatomy says.**\n","\n","* **The base switch (+16) is a different file, not a step.** The 0.95370 file is Aman Atar's; its rank correlation with\n","  the 0.95354 ladder file is far from 1, so its public noise is larger, and it has no OOF. It is the one link in the new\n","  ladders that nobody can check.\n","* **The three mixes are real moves with OOF behind them.** They are large moves (public noise SD of about 8 to 13\n","  points), and their OOF gains (+19 to +33 in-sample, +14 to +23 in the authors' nested CV) are larger than that noise\n","  and positive on all five folds. Moves of this size are something the public board *can* see, roughly.\n","* **Areeb Ali's eight probes are inside the noise.** Their public changes (-1 to +2) are all within one noise SD of\n","  zero, and the kept probe is the best of eight such numbers. On OOF the probes along `bold - balanced` gain a few\n","  points on 4 or 5 folds; scaling the whole mix gains less and less consistently, and stepping along `bold - careful`\n","  loses."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1a65dbb8","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.026476,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.160219+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.133743+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"s10\"></a>\n","<div style=\"background: #0b1f4b; color: #ffffff; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700;\">10 &middot; New in v4: \"public and CV up\" &mdash; checked fold by fold</div>\n","\n","goodpjw2008's claim is that the mixes raise **both** the public score and CV. Two checks on our replay:\n","\n","1. **Fold by fold.** A CV-confirmed step should gain on at least 4 of 5 folds, by a margin larger than the\n","   fold-to-fold spread. The mix weights saw all five folds, so these are in-sample numbers (the authors' nested\n","   numbers, with weights refitted on four folds, are shown beside them).\n","2. **Nested choice of the step size.** Areeb Ali chose *how far* to go along `bold - balanced` on the public board.\n","   Here the four other folds choose it, and the fifth scores it, for each fold in turn."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":32,"id":"f5c85ed1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.215247Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.214949Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:32:06.830815Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:32:06.829919Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.648679,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:06.835357+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:05.186678+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["nested step size along (bold - balanced): picks [1.75 1.5  1.5  1.   1.5 ]  outer gains [-3.4  3.3  4.4 19.6  4. ]  mean +5.6, up 4/5\n","the kept half step (t = 0.5): fold gains [ 1.1  2.7  3.  10.6  3. ]\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x638 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# (2) nested step size along d = bold - balanced: t chosen on four folds, scored on the fifth, gain vs the bold mix.\n","TGRID = np.round(np.arange(0, 2.01, 0.25), 2)\n","_d = PO[\"bold\"] - MO[\"balanced\"]\n","TG = np.array([[auc_sort(y[b], (PO[\"bold\"] + t * _d)[b]) for b in FOLDS] for t in TGRID]) * 1e5\n","TG = TG - TG[0]                                          # gain over bold, (t, fold)\n","T_OUT, T_PICK = np.zeros(5), np.zeros(5)\n","for f in range(5):\n","    j = TG[:, [g for g in range(5) if g != f]].mean(1).argmax(); T_PICK[f], T_OUT[f] = TGRID[j], TG[j, f]\n","print(\"nested step size along (bold - balanced): picks\", T_PICK, \" outer gains\", np.round(T_OUT, 1), f\" mean {T_OUT.mean():+.1f}, up {(T_OUT > 0).sum()}/5\")\n","print(\"the kept half step (t = 0.5): fold gains\", np.round(TG[2], 1))\n","CHK10 = [(\"careful\", \"ref\"), (\"balanced\", \"ref\"), (\"bold\", \"ref\"), (\"bold + 0.5 (bold - balanced)\", \"bold\"),\n","         (\"1.5 x bold\", \"bold\"), (\"bold + 1.5 (bold - balanced)\", \"bold\"), (\"388 + 5% GP + DVAE\", \"bold + 0.5 (bold - balanced)\"),\n","         (\"388 + 5% shallow tree\", \"bold + 0.5 (bold - balanced)\")]\n","LAB10 = {\"careful\": \"careful mix vs 0.95370\", \"balanced\": \"balanced mix vs 0.95370\", \"bold\": \"bold mix vs 0.95370\",\n","         \"bold + 0.5 (bold - balanced)\": \"0.95388 step vs bold\", \"1.5 x bold\": \"1.5 x bold vs bold\",\n","         \"bold + 1.5 (bold - balanced)\": \"bold + 1.5 (bold - bal.) vs bold\",\n","         \"388 + 5% GP + DVAE\": \"+5% GP + DVAE on 0.95388\", \"388 + 5% shallow tree\": \"+5% shallow tree on 0.95388\"}\n","V10 = []\n","for a, b in CHK10:\n","    c, d = chg(a, b); V10.append((LAB10[a], c, d, (d > 0).sum(), d.std(ddof=1)))\n","fig, (ax, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 5.8), gridspec_kw=dict(width_ratios=[1.45, 1]))\n","yy = np.arange(len(V10))[::-1]\n","for yi, (lab, c, d, up, sd) in zip(yy, V10):\n","    hold = up >= 4 and abs(c) > sd / np.sqrt(5) * 2\n","    col = CV if (hold and c > 0) else PRIV if c < 0 and up <= 1 else MUTED\n","    ax.plot([d.min(), d.max()], [yi, yi], color=RULE, lw=2.5, solid_capstyle=\"round\", zorder=1)\n","    ax.scatter(d, np.full(5, yi), s=26, color=col, alpha=0.8, edgecolor=\"none\", zorder=3)\n","    ax.plot(c, yi, \"|\", ms=16, mew=2.5, color=INK, zorder=4)\n","    ax.text(1.01, yi, f\"{c:+.1f}  {up}/5\", va=\"center\", ha=\"left\", fontsize=9, color=CVTXT if col == CV else INK2, fontweight=\"bold\" if col == CV else \"normal\",\n","            transform=ax.get_yaxis_transform(), clip_on=False)\n","ax.set_yticks(yy); ax.set_yticklabels([v[0] for v in V10], fontsize=9.5); ax.tick_params(axis=\"y\", length=0)\n","zero_line(ax, \"x\"); ax.xaxis.set_major_formatter(E5); ax.set_xlim(-14, max(v[2].max() for v in V10) + 3); ax.grid(axis=\"y\", visible=False)\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"OOF AUC change per fold (x 1e-5); black tick = change on all rows\")\n","ax.legend(handles=[Line2D([], [], marker=\"o\", ls=\"\", color=CV, label=\"holds: >= 4/5 folds, clear of the fold spread\"),\n","                   Line2D([], [], marker=\"o\", ls=\"\", color=MUTED, label=\"fold noise: small or mixed\"),\n","                   Line2D([], [], marker=\"o\", ls=\"\", color=PRIV, label=\"down on >= 4 folds\")], loc=\"upper center\", bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.16), ncol=3, fontsize=8.5)\n","panel_title(ax, \"The mixes hold on every fold; small steps are mostly fold noise\", \"five dots = five folds\")\n","for f in range(5): ax2.plot(TGRID, TG[:, f], color=C[[0, 6, 3, 4, 5][f]], lw=1.3, alpha=0.75, label=f\"fold {f}\")\n","ax2.plot(TGRID, TG.mean(1), color=INK, lw=2.4, label=\"mean of the folds\")\n","ax2.axvline(0.5, color=PUB, lw=1.2, ls=(0, (3, 2))); ax2.text(0.55, ax2.get_ylim()[1] * 0.55, \"public pick\\nt = 0.5\", color=PUB, fontsize=8.5, va=\"top\")\n","zero_line(ax2); ax2.yaxis.set_major_formatter(E5)\n","ax2.set_xlabel(\"t in  bold + t (bold - balanced)\"); ax2.set_ylabel(\"OOF change vs bold, per fold (x 1e-5)\"); ax2.legend(loc=\"upper left\", fontsize=8, ncol=2)\n","panel_title(ax2, f\"Nested step size: {T_OUT.mean():+.1f}, {(T_OUT > 0).sum()}/5 folds up\", \"inner folds pick t = \" + \", \".join(f\"{t:g}\" for t in T_PICK))\n","headline(fig, \"\\\"Public and CV up\\\" holds for the three mixes on every fold; the kept half step is small, and one fold carries about half of it\",\n","         \"OOF rows of the public files; the mix weights saw all five folds (in-sample), the step size on the right is chosen nested\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3c83feb9","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.027866,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:06.893285+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:06.865419+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"s9v\"></a>\n","### What each new notebook offers, and what its public tuning is likely to cost on private\n","\n","For every step that was **kept because it won on the board**, the public number is the best of several. The model of\n","section 4, now run on the real probes of each author: on each random 20/80 split of the OOF rows (real public and\n","private sizes), the probe with the best public gap is kept, and its private gap is read. The difference is the\n","**give-back**. A step's expected private change is its public change minus the give-back, with a 90% interval from the\n","same draws. Steps chosen without the board, or scored once, get the plain noise interval."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":33,"id":"7ddcf155","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:32:06.950621Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:32:06.950087Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:32:07.550047Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:32:07.549089Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.630962,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:07.552088+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:06.921126+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<style type=\"text/css\">\n","</style>\n","<table id=\"T_ec15f\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th id=\"T_ec15f_level0_col0\" class=\"col_heading level0 col0\" >notebook</th>\n","      <th id=\"T_ec15f_level0_col1\" class=\"col_heading level0 col1\" >step</th>\n","      <th id=\"T_ec15f_level0_col2\" class=\"col_heading level0 col2\" >public change</th>\n","      <th id=\"T_ec15f_level0_col3\" class=\"col_heading level0 col3\" >expected private change (90% interval)</th>\n","      <th id=\"T_ec15f_level0_col4\" class=\"col_heading level0 col4\" >how</th>\n","      <th id=\"T_ec15f_level0_col5\" class=\"col_heading level0 col5\" >OOF change (in-sample)</th>\n","      <th id=\"T_ec15f_level0_col6\" class=\"col_heading level0 col6\" >authors' nested</th>\n","      <th id=\"T_ec15f_level0_col7\" class=\"col_heading level0 col7\" >verdict</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <td id=\"T_ec15f_row0_col0\" class=\"data row0 col0\" >Aman Atar / goodpjw2008</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_ec15f_row0_col1\" class=\"data row0 col1\"