tack -> 0.95388 file</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row46_col1\" class=\"data row46 col1\" >by label (analysis only)</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row46_col2\" class=\"data row46 col2\" >legit rows only</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row46_col3\" class=\"data row46 col3\" >98.3%</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row46_col4\" class=\"data row46 col4\" >0.0%</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row46_col5\" class=\"data row46 col5\" >-1.2</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row46_col6\" class=\"data row46 col6\" >16.20</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row46_col7\" class=\"data row46 col7\" >-</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row47_col0\" class=\"data row47 col0\" >wide LM stack -> 0.95388 file</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row47_col1\" class=\"data row47 col1\" >by label (analysis only)</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row47_col2\" class=\"data row47 col2\" >frauds ranked below 80%</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row47_col3\" class=\"data row47 col3\" >0.1%</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row47_col4\" class=\"data row47 col4\" >7.4%</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row47_col5\" class=\"data row47 col5\" >+6.7</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row47_col6\" class=\"data row47 col6\" >18.43</td>\n","      <td id=\"T_9188b_row47_col7\" class=\"data row47 col7\" >-</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n"],"text/plain":["<pandas.io.formats.style.Styler at 0x7f5c47f26650>"]},"execution_count":37,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["# Segment table: AUC change (x 1e-5) when only the segment moves, its share of rows and frauds, how far its rows move\n","# (mean |rank change| x 1e-3), and how much more the step lifts its frauds than its legit rows (x 1e-3).\n","tab11 = SEG_TAB.copy()\n","tab11[\"rows\"] = tab11.rows.map(lambda v: f\"{v:.1%}\"); tab11[\"frauds\"] = tab11.frauds.map(lambda v: f\"{v:.1%}\")\n","tab11[\"gain\"] = tab11.gain.map(lambda v: f\"{v:+.1f}\"); tab11[\"moved\"] = tab11.moved.map(lambda v: f\"{v:.2f}\")\n","tab11[\"lift\"] = tab11.lift.map(lambda v: \"-\" if v != v else f\"{v:+.2f}\")\n","tab11 = tab11.rename(columns={\"gain\": \"AUC change if only it moves\", \"moved\": \"mean |rank change|\", \"lift\": \"frauds minus legit shift\"})\n","tab11.style.hide(axis=\"index\") if hasattr(tab11.style, \"hide\") else tab11"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"46926043","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.034792,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:09.483873+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:09.449081+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What the error analysis says** (all on the OOF stand-in, so a guide rather than a forecast):\n","\n","* **The top 1% is settled.** All four files catch the same share of frauds in their top 1%, 2% and 5% of rows (to a\n","  tenth of a percent). The steps between them hardly touch the order of the top rows.\n","* **The mixes gain lower down.** The step from the 0.95370 replay to the bold mix gains almost all of its AUC in rows\n","  the replay ranks *below* its top 5%: about a quarter of all frauds sit there, and the mix lifts them clearly more\n","  than the legit rows around them (left rank-shift panel). Its members carry signal about frauds that the base file\n","  ranks too low, which is also why the gain shows on every fold.\n","* **The change is spread over many rows.** The 1% of rows that move furthest are almost all legit rows in the middle\n","  of the score; they carry only a small part of the gain, and half of the rows must take the new ranks before most of\n","  it appears. These are not a few lucky rows.\n","* **The honest stack is still ahead on OOF.** Moving from the wide LM stack to the 0.95388 file's OOF counterpart\n","  loses, and again the loss sits below the top 1%, mostly in the 80&ndash;99% bands. The replay\n","  is an approximation (about 1% of the 0.95370 file has no OOF counterpart, and goodpjw2008 notes that the replay is\n","  if anything too hard on the file), so this is a measured hint, not a verdict on the file.\n","* **Calibration of the order.** A step that helps does not shift every fraud up; it shifts frauds up *relative to\n","  legit rows of the same band*. The rank-shift panels show that gap band by band. They are a description, not the\n","  whole story: in the third panel the 0.95388 file lifts low-ranked frauds more than legit rows *on average* and still\n","  loses AUC against the wide stack, because the AUC counts how many legit rows each fraud ends up above, row by row,\n","  not the average move."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1a44ffc2","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.034742,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:09.552049+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:09.517307+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"s12\"></a>\n","<div style=\"background: #0b1f4b; color: #ffffff; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700;\">12 &middot; New in v4: can one honest step improve the best public file?</div>\n","\n","This notebook's `submission.csv` starts from the best public file, **Areeb Ali's 0.95388**, rebuilt from public inputs\n","above. On top of it we allow **at most two steps**, and only steps that pass a rule fixed before looking at any result:\n","\n","1. **Candidates.** A small step `B + w (M - B)` in logit-rank space towards (or away from) one public member `M` that\n","   has honest OOF on the shared five folds and is **not** one of the 87 members already in the mix: the 17 single\n","   models of mathsonchain's dataset, goodpjw2008's wide stack without LMs and his EBM bag. `w` is one of\n","   &plusmn;0.01, &plusmn;0.02, &plusmn;0.03, &plusmn;0.05. That is 152 candidate steps.\n","2. **Nested choice.** For each of the five folds in turn, the other four folds pick the best candidate (member and\n","   weight); the held-out fold scores it.\n","3. **Gate.** Accept a step only if it gains on **at least 4 of 5** held-out folds and on average. The public board is\n","   never consulted.\n","\n","If no step passes, the output is the plain rebuild of the 0.95388 file."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":38,"id":"f929d96a","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:32:09.622251Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:32:09.621798Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:32:10.006747Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:32:10.005919Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.424502,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:10.010232+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:09.58573+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x528 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, (ax, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4.8), gridspec_kw=dict(width_ratios=[1.35, 1]))\n","rd = EXT[0]\n","cols = [CV if g > 0 else PRIV for g in rd[\"outer\"]]\n","ax.bar(np.arange(5), rd[\"outer\"], color=cols, width=0.6, zorder=3)\n","for f, (g, (m, w)) in enumerate(zip(rd[\"outer\"], rd[\"picks\"])):\n","    ax.text(f, g + (0.4 if g >= 0 else -0.4), f\"{g:+.1f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\" if g >= 0 else \"top\", fontsize=10, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK)\n","ylo = min(rd[\"outer\"].min(), 0) - 4.5; yhi = max(rd[\"outer\"].max(), 0) + 3\n","ax.set_ylim(ylo, yhi)\n","for f, (m, w) in enumerate(rd[\"picks\"]):\n","    ax.text(f, ylo + 0.4, f\"{m.split(' (')[0]}\\nw = {w:+.2f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=7.8, color=INK2)\n","zero_line(ax); ax.set_xticks(range(5)); ax.set_xticklabels([f\"held-out fold {f}\" for f in range(5)], fontsize=9)\n","ax.yaxis.set_major_formatter(E5); ax.set_ylabel(\"AUC change on the held-out fold (x 1e-5)\"); ax.grid(axis=\"x\", visible=False)\n","panel_title(ax, f\"Step 1: up on {(rd['outer'] > 0).sum()} of 5 held-out folds, mean {rd['outer'].mean():+.1f}: \"\n","                f\"{'PASSES' if rd['passed'] else 'does not pass'} the gate\", \"the step each set of four folds picked (bottom) and how it did on the fifth\")\n","vals = [rd[\"final_in\"], rd[\"outer\"].mean()]\n","ax2.bar([0, 1], vals, color=[MUTED, CV if vals[1] > 0 else PRIV], width=0.55, zorder=3)\n","for i, v in enumerate(vals): ax2.text(i, v + (0.25 if v >= 0 else -0.25), f\"{v:+.1f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\" if v >= 0 else \"top\", fontsize=11, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK)\n","zero_line(ax2); ax2.set_xticks([0, 1]); ax2.set_xticklabels([\"best of 152 steps,\\nchosen and scored\\non the same five folds\", \"the same search,\\nnested (chosen on four,\\nscored on the fifth)\"], fontsize=9)\n","ax2.yaxis.set_major_formatter(E5); ax2.set_ylabel(\"OOF change (x 1e-5)\"); ax2.grid(axis=\"x\", visible=False)\n","lo2 = min(vals) - 2; ax2.set_ylim(min(lo2, -2), max(vals) + 2)\n","panel_title(ax2, \"Selection inflates CV too\", \"the winner's curse of section 4, inside cross-validation\")\n","headline(fig, \"No candidate step passes the nested gate: the output stays the plain rebuild of the 0.95388 file\" if N_STEPS == 0\n","         else f\"{N_STEPS} step(s) pass the nested gate and are applied on top of the 0.95388 file\",\n","         \"152 small steps towards or away from 19 public members with honest OOF, chosen inside the folds; the public board is never used\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":39,"id":"c7089a61","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-14T10:32:10.086398Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-14T10:32:10.085733Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-14T10:32:10.196247Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-14T10:32:10.195189Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.151721,"end_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:10.198634+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-14T10:32:10.046913+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["rebuild of the best public file (0.95388, Areeb Ali) identical to the published one: True\n","extension steps that passed the nested gate: 0\n","  round 1: held-out gains [  5.2 -10.3   1.5   3.1  -6.5], up on 3/5, me